Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gives it a better soak?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats what matter does, im talking about a prime enchantment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-16T10:00:30-08:00","id":1548532,"title":"","content":"They've made it clear since the first edition, yes. The first example I remember reading was a Etherite who gave their street clothes the same armor value as twelve inch thick steel plate. They used a Matter/Prime working to transfer the armor value from the battleship scrap to the clothing. <br /> <br /> Did I help you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-16T10:23:12-08:00","id":1548533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548527-enchanting-armor?p=1548532#post1548532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've made it clear since the first edition, yes. The first example I remember reading was a Etherite who gave their street clothes the same armor value as twelve inch thick steel plate. They used a Matter/Prime working to transfer the armor value from the battleship scrap to the clothing.<br /> <br /> Did I help you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, i want know what pure prime 2 enchantment does for armor,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-16T11:36:09-08:00","id":1548534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548527-enchanting-armor?p=1548533#post1548533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, i want know what pure prime 2 enchantment does for armor,</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-16T15:31:30-08:00","id":1548538,"title":"","content":"With Prime 2 you can enchant armor to work against the attacks of spirits. Since the sphere description also mentions aggravated damage, it might allow the armor rating to apply as soak against damage from direct magical attacks, not just physical things like fire or the claws and teeth of supernatural creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-16T15:51:55-08:00","id":1548539,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the big benefit of straight Prime boosting armor is increasing its versatility against non-physical attacks. How much so is kinda variable by edition, but broadly the idea is that armor might be able to soak, say, a werewolf's claws, but might not be able to soak fire or radiation unless specifically designed to do so. So using Matter to have Armor 8 street clothes is great against lots of Agg attacks, but still doesn't protect you from anything that straight up ignores armor anyway.<br /> <br /> Prime enchanted armor is closer to the platonic ideal of &quot;protection,&quot; and is thus less easily circumvented (again, what this means is not consistent in the game line); but most generally seems to mean &quot;purely supernatural attacks that wouldn't be blocked by armor because it lacks a physical aspect.&quot;<br /> <br /> While not really well aligned with most of the modern day interpretations of things, Sorcerer's Crusade as the signature Hermetic protection spell something one could attach to physical armor, but could just use on yourself too. Instead of Prime enchantment akin to making weapons more deadly, it functions as an extension of counter-magic. Basically, the spell lets you spend 1 quintessence to reduce the success of a magical (not just Awakened) offensive attack on you on a 1-for-1 basis reflexively rather than having to use active countermagic. Sort of a precursor to modern day Mage games that have magical countermagic materials as a more common approach to this. Combining the ability to simply nullify effects thrown at you with Prime's ability to increase your Quintessence pool significantly, it's a potent and IMO far more interesting approach than just &quot;can soak better.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T14:27:52-08:00","id":1548600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548527-enchanting-armor#post1548527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enchanting weapons makes them deal aggro damage. But what does enchanting armor do? Normal armor already can soak aggro damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only certain armors can soak certain types of aggravated damage. Also it's not just armor that can be infused this way. Prime 2 just says substances, so regular clothing can be made to soak aggravated damage and spirit attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T16:03:44-08:00","id":1548603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1548527-enchanting-armor?p=1548600#post1548600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only certain armors can soak certain types of aggravated damage. Also it's not just armor that can be infused this way. Prime 2 just says substances, so regular clothing can be made to soak aggravated damage and spirit attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by certain forms of aggrovated damage? Lets say we have a breastplate, it is enchanted. Does it stop electricity from going thorugh the metal? does it somehow stop a flamethrower even though it protects just the chest? does it stop locked direct damage spells?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T06:31:48-08:00","id":1548613,"title":"","content":"One of the examples in Mage is that combat armor might be able to soak a bite, and therefore a vampire bite, but it can't soak fire.<br /> <br /> I would rule that Prime enhanced armor can soak any source of damage that tries to pass through it. I would also, purely from the standpoint of running a game, assume that any narrow attack (that is one that doesn't have a wide area of effect) passes through the armor unless the attacker aims otherwise. That second one is purely a convenient assumption to keep calculation simple.<br /> <br /> So, I would have quint enhanced armor capable of soaking fire, though the flamethrower would be too wide an attack to completely block. It would block the electricity, narrower sources of fire, and any attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}